# The rule this file follows
#
# Tracked:   everything a result can be rebuilt or checked from — manifests, run registries,
#            campaign histories, and the derived tables and figures a document cites by name.
# Ignored:   per-run scratch output, logs, caches, environments, and derived artefacts of probes
#            and fixtures that no document refers to.
#
# The distinction is deliberately not "generated vs. handwritten". A run registry is generated and
# is tracked, because regenerating it costs 5,248 core hours. A probe figure is generated and is
# ignored, because regenerating it costs a minute.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling and environments
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
analysis/.venv/
analysis/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
analysis/notebooks/.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Python test artefacts
.pytest_cache/
.pytest_tmp*/
**/__pycache__/

# Codex session scratch (codex exec logs)
.codex_tmp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
outputs/
debug_results/
fit*.csv
fit*.png
benchmarks/results/
benchmarks/odeformer/results/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# experiments/ — the per-run files are scratch, the registry and history are evidence
#
# runs/ holds one directory per cell and reaches 16 MB for Phase B alone; it is reproducible
# from the registry plus the image. run_registry.csv and history.jsonl are NOT reproducible
# without re-running the campaign and are therefore tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
experiments/*/runs/
experiments/*/run.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# analysis/ — derived data, tables and figures
#
# Ignored by default; the two named experiment identifiers are tracked because CLAUDE.md,
# PAPER_1.md and the paper sections cite those artefacts by name. Probe and fixture outputs
# (wp_a2_*, wp_a4_*, wp_n2_*, ...) stay out.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
analysis/data/*
!analysis/data/.gitkeep
!analysis/data/paper1_phaseB_v1/
!analysis/data/paper1_phaseC_v1/
!analysis/data/wp_n1_dim2_probe/
!analysis/data/wp_t1_term_relevance/
!analysis/data/wp_t1b_standalone_ranking/
# ... but not the per-cell evaluation rows and the full selection path: both are
# deterministic and rebuildable from the hashed inputs plus the configuration hash.
analysis/data/wp_t1b_standalone_ranking/details.csv
analysis/data/wp_t1b_standalone_ranking/selection_path.csv
# ... but not its 11 MB per-equation records: deterministic, and rebuildable from
# the hashed inputs plus the configuration hash in run_metadata.json.
analysis/data/wp_t1_term_relevance/records.csv

analysis/figures/*
!analysis/figures/.gitkeep
!analysis/figures/paper1_phaseA_v1/
!analysis/figures/paper1_phaseB_v1/
!analysis/figures/paper1_phaseC_v1/

analysis/tables/*
!analysis/tables/.gitkeep
!analysis/tables/paper1_phaseA_v1/
!analysis/tables/paper1_phaseB_v1/
!analysis/tables/paper1_phaseC_v1/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Kubernetes manifests with a substituted commit SHA, produced at launch time from k8s/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/phase_b_bootstrap.yaml
/phase_b_cells.yaml

# pytest scratch
.tmp/
